%% Crash recovery sequence — companion to PDF Figure 3

sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Client
    participant API as API Server
    participant Sup as Supervisor
    participant WA as Worker A (active)
    participant WB as Worker B (warm)

    Note over Client,WB: Steady state: Worker A streaming a request to Client

    WA-xWA: SIGSEGV / STATUS_ACCESS_VIOLATION
    Note right of WA: T+0

    Sup-->>Sup: kqueue / JobObject notifies of exit
    Note right of Sup: T+20ms — capture exit code

    Sup->>API: WorkerLost(worker_id, [in_flight_ids])
    Sup->>API: WorkerPromote(Worker_B)
    Note right of Sup: T+30-80ms

    API-->>API: consult retry policy per request
    Note right of API: T+80-150ms

    alt non-streaming, idempotent
        API->>WB: re-dispatch InferenceJob
        WB-->>API: InferenceDone
        API-->>Client: 200 OK (client never saw an error)
    else streaming, 0 tokens emitted
        API->>WB: re-dispatch InferenceJob
        API->>Client: event: retry
        WB-->>API: InferenceTokenBatch (resumed)
        API->>Client: event: token (normal)
    else streaming, ≥1 token emitted
        API->>Client: event: error<br/>{ code: "WORKER_CRASHED_MID_STREAM",<br/>  recoverable: true,<br/>  resume_token: ... }
        Note over Client: Client may POST /v1/inference/resume
    end

    Note right of WB: T+280ms — first token from Worker B

    Sup->>Sup: spawn replacement warm worker
    Note right of Sup: T+500ms — write crashdump async (5/min rate limit)
